@page "/docs/components/toast"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Toast
<PageTitle>Toast - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Toast</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="toast" />
        </div>
        <p>Notifications you raise from C# through an injected service, with no markup at the call site. Toasts stack at an edge of the screen, spread apart on hover, close on their own after a delay and can be swiped away. A single call can also follow an async operation, showing a spinner that resolves in place to success or error.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock SetupSnippet="Toast/UsageSetup" Example="typeof(ToastDefaultExample)"
                Description="Register the service and the host once, then inject `IToastService` into any component or service and call it to raise a toast." />

    @* Setup and API are reference, not examples: plain code sections (no preview frame to leave
       empty) and h2s, so the TOC lists them beside Usage instead of nesting them under Examples. *@
    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Setup</h2>
        <p>Register the service once and place a single host at the root of your app.</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="Toast/Setup" />
        <p>This docs app is already set up this way, with <code>AddBlaizio()</code> in <code>Program.cs</code> and one <code>&lt;ToastProvider /&gt;</code> in the layout, so every demo below is live.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">API</h2>
        <p>Inject <code>IToastService</code> wherever you need it and call one of these methods:</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="Toast/IToastService" />
    </section>

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="A one-line message that closes on its own after the default duration." Example="typeof(ToastDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With description" Description="Set `Description` to add a secondary line under the title." Example="typeof(ToastDescriptionExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Types" Description="Success, error, warning and info each get their own icon. A loading toast shows a spinner and stays on screen until you resolve it." Example="typeof(ToastTypesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Rich colors" Description="Set `RichColors` to fill the whole toast with the color of its type." Example="typeof(ToastRichColorsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Action button" Description="An `Action` adds a primary button that runs your handler and then closes the toast." Example="typeof(ToastActionExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Cancel button" Description="A `Cancel` adds a secondary button. This example pairs it with a close button." Example="typeof(ToastCancelExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Track an async operation" Description="`Track` shows one toast with a spinner while the task runs, then turns it into a success or error toast in place when the task completes." Example="typeof(ToastTrackExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom content" Description="Pass a `RenderFragment` instead of a title when the toast body needs your own markup." Example="typeof(ToastCustomContentExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom icon" Description="Set `Icon` to replace the icon on a single toast. To change the loading spinner everywhere, set `LoadingIcon` on the provider, for example to a spinning Tabler icon." Example="typeof(ToastIconExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Close button" Description="`CloseButton` adds a close button at the end of the toast. Set it on a single toast, or on the `ToastProvider` to make it the default." Example="typeof(ToastCloseExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom duration" Description="Set `Duration` to change how long a toast stays, or `Persistent` to keep it until it is dismissed." Example="typeof(ToastDurationExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Position" Description="Set `Position` on a toast to open it somewhere other than the `ToastProvider` default: any corner, or the center of the top or bottom edge." Example="typeof(ToastPositionExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Update and dismiss" Description="Every call returns an id. Pass it back to update that toast in place, or pass it to `Dismiss` to close it." Example="typeof(ToastUpdateExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization" Description="Combine the options to brand a toast. This success toast uses a custom `Icon`, rich colors and a description. For a body built from your own markup, see Custom content." Example="typeof(ToastCustomizationExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Toasts follow the reading direction of the app, and `Direction` sets it for a single toast. Here a right-to-left toast opens on this left-to-right page, with the icon, buttons and text mirrored." Example="typeof(ToastRtlExample)" />

</div>

